# ============================================================
# Line endings are load-bearing for binary/artifact files.
#
# C1 (ML audit): with core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, git
# rewrote the LightGBM boosters (*.txt) to CRLF on checkout.
# lgb.Booster(model_file=...) then logs "Model format error, expect a
# tree here" and calls Log::Fatal, which ABORTS the process
# (exit -1073740791). That is a native abort, not a Python
# exception, so the serving fallback cannot catch it: /forecast
# hard-crashes the worker and pytest segfaults.
#
# Model artifacts are text formats with a line-oriented parser, so
# they must never be CRLF-normalised.
# ============================================================
backend/ml/artifacts/*.txt   -text
backend/ml/artifacts/*.json  -text
backend/ml/artifacts/*.joblib binary

# Source and config: normalise to LF in the repo, checkout as-is.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf